-- 11. Warning Letter (disciplinary)
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
(NULL, 'warning_letter', 'Warning Letter', E'NIKKI TECHNOLOGIES\n\nDate: {{today}}\n\nTo,\n{{name}}\n{{designation}} — {{segment}}\nEmployee ID: {{staff_code}}\n\nSubject: Written Warning\n\nDear {{name}},\n\nThis letter is to formally record a concern regarding the following:\n\n  [HR: describe the specific incident, date, and the standard or policy concerned. Be factual and specific. Remove this instruction before issuing.]\n\nThis conduct is not in keeping with the standards expected under our Code of Conduct and the terms of your appointment.\n\nYou are advised to ensure that this is not repeated. Specifically, we expect the following corrective action:\n\n  [HR: state what must change, and by when. Remove this instruction before issuing.]\n\nPlease note that any repetition of such conduct may result in further disciplinary action, which may include termination of employment.\n\nIf you wish to respond to this warning, or believe the facts recorded here are incorrect, you may submit a written response to HR within seven (7) days. Your response will be placed on record alongside this letter.\n\nWe would like to see this matter resolved and are willing to support you in doing so.\n\nFor Nikki Technologies\n\n_______________________\nAuthorised Signatory\n\nAcknowledgement of receipt by employee (acknowledging receipt does not mean you agree with the contents):\n\nEmployee: {{name}}\nDate: {{today}}', true),

